Third-party software in the published images
--------------------------------------------
Every image is assembled from Wolfi packages (https://packages.wolfi.dev), each under its upstream
license; the Wolfi build recipes are Apache License 2.0 (https://github.com/wolfi-dev/os). The SPDX
SBOM attached to every image and every GitHub release lists the license of each package. Among
them:

- Node.js: MIT License.
- glibc: LGPL-2.1-or-later. OpenSSL: Apache License 2.0. ICU: Unicode License.
- In the development images also: busybox (GPL-2.0-only), bash (GPL-3.0-or-later),
  git (GPL-2.0-only), GCC (GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception), Python (PSF).

Source code for the GPL and LGPL packages is available from their upstream projects and from the
Wolfi build recipes, which name the exact upstream source and version of every package. On request,
we provide the corresponding source of any package in an image we published, for three years after
that image's release.

